### Please describe the problem in your own words.

Trying to "git annex get" from a SSH remote can fail when filenames contain some Unicode characters such as U+3000 IDEOGRAPHIC SPACE, which is the default whitespace character when inputting Japanese text.

### What steps will reproduce the problem?

```
export GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=test@example.com GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=test@example.com
git init a; cd a; git annex init
echo x > 'foo　bar'   # U+3000 between foo and bar
git annex add; git commit -m add; cd ..
git clone ssh://localhost$PWD/a b; cd b; git annex init
git annex get .
```

The last command will fail with

```
get "foo\343\200\200bar" (from origin...)

  Transfer failed

  Unable to access these remotes: origin

  No other repository is known to contain the file.
failed
get: 1 failed
```

### What version of git-annex are you using? On what operating system?

git-annex version: 10.20260421 on NixOS/Linux.

### Please provide any additional information below.

Claude produced this patch, which I don't understand, but when running "git annex get" with this patch succeeds, so maybe it is useful.

```patch
--- a/P2P/Protocol.hs	2026-10-26 12:16:18.311257773 +0100
+++ b/P2P/Protocol.hs	2026-10-26 12:16:29.446642504 +0100
@@ -221,14 +221,17 @@
 -- unlikely to care about spaces vs tabs or control characters.
 instance Proto.Serializable ProtoAssociatedFile where
 	serialize (ProtoAssociatedFile (AssociatedFile Nothing)) = ""
-	serialize (ProtoAssociatedFile (AssociatedFile (Just af))) = 
-		fromOsPath $ toInternalGitPath $
-			OS.concat $ map esc $ OS.unpack af
+	serialize (ProtoAssociatedFile (AssociatedFile (Just af))) =
+		-- Escape after decoding to unicode, not per byte. The peer
+		-- splits the line with a unicode isSpace, so multibyte
+		-- whitespace (eg U+3000) must be escaped, while utf-8
+		-- continuation bytes (eg 0xA0, 0x85) must not be.
+		concatMap esc (fromOsPath (toInternalGitPath af) :: String)
 	  where
-	  	esc c = case OS.toChar c of
-			'%' -> literalOsPath "%%"
-			c' | isSpace c' -> literalOsPath "%"
-			_ -> OS.singleton c
+	  	esc '%' = "%%"
+		esc c
+			| isSpace c = "%"
+			| otherwise = [c]
 	
 	deserialize s = case fromInternalGitPath $ toOsPath $ deesc [] s of
 		f
```

### Have you had any luck using git-annex before? (Sometimes we get tired of reading bug reports all day and a lil' positive end note does wonders)

I've spend the last few days migrating *everything* to git annex, it's wonderful!

